  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\n# tag: LTS_MM_YYYY_RefRR --> version: YYYY.MM.refRR\n# The Git tags originally used the format YYYY-MM-DD, which we adopted for this\n# recipe. More recent tags are no longer consistent (eg LTS_07_2022_Ref02). To\n# ensure that the latest version is always installed, we created the version\n# string as a rearrangement of the tag name: LTS_MM_YYYY_RefRR --> YYYY.MM.refRR\n#\n# This matches the scheme azure-c-shared-utility uses, so the two stay\n# consistent. Note that `refRR` parses as a string component and therefore\n# sorts below the bare version (2022.07.ref02 < 2022.07); harmless here, as\n# every upstream tag carries a RefRR and a plain YYYY.MM is never published.\n#\n# Releases: https://github.com/Azure/azure-uamqp-c/tags\ncontext:\n  name: azure-uamqp-c\n  version: \"2022.07.ref02\"\n  tag: LTS_07_2022_Ref02\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://github.com/Azure/azure-uamqp-c/archive/${{ tag }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: f086b1b0bbfd098749ce960d2e04f481dd6e51e580236a3f8a8238eed0bbd294\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: not win64\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n  host:\n    - azure-c-shared-utility\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(name, upper_bound='x.x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      files:\n        - Library/bin/uamqp.dll\n        - Library/lib/uamqp.lib\n\nabout:\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: uAMQP is a general purpose C library for AMQP 1.0.\n  homepage: https://github.com/Azure/azure-uamqp-c\n  repository: https://github.com/Azure/azure-uamqp-c\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - xylar\n    - seanyen\n",
